### BLE Services

All projects use standardised Nakomis ESP32 UUIDs (compatible with sandboxsite and any conforming web/mobile client):

```cpp
#define NAKOMIS_ESP32_SERVICE_UUID        "4fafc201-1fb5-459e-8fcc-c5c9c331914b"
#define NAKOMIS_ESP32_CHARACTERISTIC_UUID "beb5483e-36e1-4688-b7f5-ea07361b26a8"
```

**BLE Commands (JSON):**
```json
// WiFi Configuration
{"command":"wifi_config","ssid":"...","password":"..."}
{"command":"wifi_connect"}
{"command":"wifi_status"}

// OTA Update
{"command":"ota_update","url":"https://..."}
{"command":"ota_status"}
```

## OTA Update Flow

1. User connects to the device from a BLE client (e.g. sandboxsite, or a project-specific UI)
2. User configures WiFi via BLE (if needed)
3. User selects firmware version
4. Client sends OTA command with signed S3 URL
5. Device shuts down BLE to free memory
6. Device downloads firmware to `/firmware_update.bin` on SD card
7. Device reboots
8. Bootloader detects update file, flashes to OTA partition
9. Bootloader deletes update file, boots main app

